SID Range Meaning <code>&lt; 100</code> Reserved <code>100 - 999999</code> Standard/community rules <code>&gt;= 1000000</code> Local custom rules <p>For your own rules, use:</p> <pre><code>sid:1000001;
</code></pre> <p>Increment <code>rev</code> when you update a rule:</p> <pre><code>rev:2;
</code></pre>

Task Flag Description User enumeration <code>-e u</code> Enumerates valid usernames All plugins <code>-e ap</code> Enumerates all detectable plugins Vulnerable plugins <code>-e vp</code> Shows vulnerable plugins Vulnerable themes <code>-e vt</code> Shows vulnerable themes Aggressive plugin detection <code>--plugins-detection aggressive</code> Brute-forces plugin paths <p>Example scan:</p> <pre><code>wpscan --url http://blog.inlanefreight.com -e u,ap
</code></pre> <p>With an API token:</p> <pre><code>wpscan --url http://blog.inlanefreight.com -e vp,vt --api-token &lt;TOKEN&gt;
</code></pre> <p>The API token is required to map detected components to known vulnerabilities.</p>
